    "prompt": "Use case: stylized-concept. Asset type: original fan-made production sprite sheet for a side-view tactical video game, faithful to Metal Gear Solid V The Phantom Pain (1984). EXACTLY 4 columns by 4 rows, exactly 16 independently DRAWN full-body poses of ONE same character. Pure flat magenta #FF00FF canvas with five thin continuous pure cyan #00FFFF vertical grid lines and five horizontal grid lines, including outer boundaries. Each equal square cell must contain exactly one complete character, wholly inside, generous empty margin at least 30 pixels, no extremity or equipment on guides. Fixed camera, strict orthographic RIGHT-facing profile, feet bottom aligned, identical physical scale every frame. Detailed crisp military pixel art, clear small-scale silhouette, no scenery, no ground shadow, no text, no labels, no logos, no watermark. The sixteen poses must be genuinely different drawings, never simple shifted duplicates. Four phases per row in left-to-right time order, preserve all costume and identity features in EVERY pose. Keep weapons and hands compact inside their cell. Subject: Pequod, the Diamond Dogs helicopter support pilot from MGSV TPP, as a restrained ORIGINAL FAN-MADE anonymous aircrew interpretation matching this project's existing codec pilot portrait, NOT a claim of a uniquely canonical face. Adult male pilot with short brown hair/stubble, weathered muted brown flight helmet, black/dark visor goggles resting above face, padded earcups, black boom microphone. Olive zipped flight suit with high cloth collar, harness/black webbing straps, olive utility pockets, dark flight gloves, sturdy dark brown boots. No eyepatch or bandana, no Snake horns, no character emblems/text. Row1 four calm flightcrew idle stages standing alert. Row2 four compact right-facing walking gait stages heel-contact/compression/passing/opposite-contact. Row3 four touching helmet earcup to answer radio then lowering hand, genuine arm articulation. Row4 four defensive crouch/recover phases, no panic marks, no particles, no weapon or firing. Same anonymous pilot identity throughout, all16 fullbody figures strict right-facing profile.",
